---
import { ArrowRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import { sitePath } from '../../lib/routes';
---

<section class="intro-overview" aria-labelledby="intro-overview-heading">
    <div class="intro-overview__heading">
        <div>
            <p class="section-kicker">Why two systems?</p>
            <h2 id="intro-overview-heading">Two old authorities. One age of warlords.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
            By the Sengoku period, Japan still recognized both the ancient Imperial
            Court and the Muromachi warrior government even as regional daimyo held
            increasing military and territorial power.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="intro-overview__title-note">
        <p class="intro-overview__jp" lang="ja">信長の野望・天下創世</p>
        <div>
            <p class="section-kicker">The Japanese title</p>
            <h3><em>Tenka Sōsei</em> — “Genesis of the Realm”</h3>
            <p>
                <em>Rise to Power</em> is the English release title. “Genesis of the
                Realm” is a contextual rendering of <em>Tenka Sōsei</em>: <em>tenka</em>
                evokes the realm or “all under heaven,” while <em>sōsei</em> means
                creation or genesis.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="intro-overview__logic" aria-label="How the two game systems relate to historical authority">
        <article>
            <span class="intro-overview__seal" aria-hidden="true">官</span>
            <p class="section-kicker">Imperial recognition</p>
            <h3>Ranks <small>(game term)</small></h3>
            <p>
                <em>Rise to Power</em> folds two historical concepts into one gameplay
                ladder: <strong>位階</strong> (court rank) and <strong>官職</strong>
                (court office). Historically they were distinct. Offices had a
                conventional corresponding rank, but an individual holder’s actual
                位階 did not have to match the office’s nominal place in that scheme.
            </p>
            <strong>Politics ↑</strong>
        </article>
        <span class="intro-overview__plus" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        <article>
            <span class="intro-overview__seal" aria-hidden="true">将</span>
            <p class="section-kicker">Shogunal recognition</p>
            <h3>Titles</h3>
            <p>Offices and appointments associated with the warrior government.</p>
            <strong>Leadership ↑</strong>
        </article>
    </div>

    <div class="intro-overview__example">
        <div>
            <p class="section-kicker">One province, two appointments</p>
            <h3>Mutsu makes the distinction visible.</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="intro-overview__comparison">
            <div>
                <strong>Governor of Mutsu</strong>
                <span lang="ja">陸奥守</span>
                <small>Imperial Court office → Rank</small>
            </div>
            <div>
                <strong>Shugo of Mutsu</strong>
                <span lang="ja">陸奥守護</span>
                <small>Shogunate appointment → Title</small>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <a class="intro-overview__more" href={sitePath('trivia/context/')}>
        <span>Read the full political context</span>
        <ArrowRight size={15} stroke-width={1.9} aria-hidden="true" />
    </a>
</section>
